hi I'm Evan Carmichael welcome to  another edition of ask Evan in today's  episode I'm going to answer question  from one of my newsletter readers of  sand ax who wrote in about asking about  getting funding for a Youth Center so  the question was thank you every for the  past few months have been thinking of  opening a new center in our area I plan  to speak where the word counselor I  don't have any finances right now we're  thinking of asking for sponsorships and  donations what are the things that  should be aware before I take any  further steps so thank you for the  question great noble vision that you  have here to create this Youth Center a  couple of ideas for you the first thing  I would do is have a big vision let's  start small so instead of going after a  youth center which might be really  timely you know costly you know a whole  set of problems that you'll come into  trying to create this youth center and  it may frustrate you the point of  wanting to quit start with something  smaller start with a few simple events  community events that target youth and  you know build up some momentum from  those events and so you know it's easy  to show that what you're doing works  there's a reason behind it you have an  impact and then when you go to you know  build your the community center you have  some momentum behind you so that'd be my  first step is try to start on a small  scale have that big vision but start  small and start with something that's  low cost easy to set up and you can  start making an impact in the community  right away it also be rewarding for you  that you can see hey you're actually  making a difference and it doesn't  necessarily need to have a huge  community center you can do things on a  really small scale and still impact  people's lives and that will give you  the juice and the momentum and the  encouragement to want to go out and do  it more and more and more and more and  more you know when I started helping  entrepreneurs I did it just ad hoc small  scale helping individual entrepreneurs  and I've had a couple of events and it  got me hooked and I've got to do more of  this I love it gonna really expand it  and give me the fuel to want to keep  going so if you start small do a couple  things small events you can see is  having an impact it'll give you the  motivation to to want to keep going and  doing it more  the next thing if you're trying to  target sponsorship I would definitely  have a laser targeted focus so what is  it that you are trying to do or try to  get kids off the street are you trying  to encourage them to learn a certain  skill set what is the goal or the vision  of your enterprise so that would really  help a lot of people have you know mixed  bag of goals and vision that's hard to  communicate the harder it is to explain  what it is that you do and the benefits  you're going to be able to provide the  harder it is for somebody to jump on  board and want to sponsor you and or be  a customer be a partner right so you  have to really have a clear message and  the laser targeted focus on what it is  that you're doing and the reason for  your existence so you may already know  that you didn't explain it you know in  the email you sent but in all your  communications now you also want to say  here's why I'm doing this and here's  what we're gonna do to make it really  clear and then it helps you know anybody  who you're talking to you think about  ways to potentially help you so if you  just say I'm open in a Youth Center you  know there's a lot of different ways to  potentially help but if you had a  specific focus then it's gonna be easier  for people to jump on board and you may  not know that yet that's fine but before  you go start talking to companies I  definitely have that laser focus and in  the last thing I touched on that already  but it's build momentum so as much as  you can you want to show that you're not  just starting up it's really hard for  companies and for anybody really to want  to back somebody who's just getting  started  because there's so many people who start  up who aren't really serious who don't  commit to it and their enterprise falls  apart and so you need to show that  you're the one who's actually going to  succeed and you're really committed to  this and you're really going to make  sure that it happens so you can start as  I said small with the events you know  show that it's working help people out  you know sure that you can have a  meaningful impact but it'll expand on  that and try to get you know some  activity going on Facebook and YouTube  and build up a newsletter list as much  as you can to build momentum and show  that people are behind this try to get  some advisors who are maybe a little  well known in your community who can  lend their name to the project as well  so that way when you go to your sponsors  potential customers here you're able to  show them hey let me put on a couple of  bands we've had a great impact we're  building up a following on Facebook and  YouTube we have our new  we've got these local people who are  advisors to the business to the the  corporation that's something that then  somebody can look at a business can look  and say hey we want to get behind we  should be involved in this or if you  just go with an idea with zero track  record and zero momentum you're probably  gonna get a no and that just comes from  my experience in a venture capital  business you know I looked at I don't  know how many business plans too many  business plans and we rejected 99% of  them a lot of the times was because they  had zero momentum behind them just an  idea on paper is not enough to get  somebody to want to put money into your  company so you have to show them that  you've got something happening here that  they're gonna be missing out on the  opportunity and that there's this is  real you're not just the average  everyday startup who's gonna launch an  idea because they had a you know a dream  one night and then they shot it down the  next week  that's the biggest fear that people will  have but you'll just go and spend their  money and you won't be able to show them  a return so if you're already having an  impact then you're using that money to  fuel it even more and have a greater  impact so hopefully that helps if you  guys liked the video for those of you  watching I'd love it if you can give it  a thumbs up it always makes my day and  makes me want to do more of these videos  for you guys and if you have a comment  I'd love to hear from you or if you have  a question for me as well just leave it  in the comments below I'll be sure to  read and get back to you so thank you  and we'll see you on the next episode  you
 

